@startuml
title Configure Internal Services (Library, Parking, Canteen) for Wallet

|Service Owner|
start
:Identify need for new internal service\n(e.g. Library Fine, Parking Pass, Canteen Package);
:Submit request to System Admin\n(outside system: email/meeting);

|System Admin|
:Receive service configuration request;
:Log in to admin portal;
:Select "Manage services & service groups";

|Admin Portal|
:Request current service list\nfrom Wallet System;

|Wallet System|
:Fetch all internal services\n(library, parking, canteen, etc.);
:Return list to Admin Portal;

|Admin Portal|
:Display current service list;

|System Admin|
:Choose action (Add new service / Edit existing service);

if (Add new service?) then (yes)
  :Enter service code, name,\ncategory (LIBRARY / PARKING / CANTEEN / OTHER),
  unit owner, default price rules;
  |Admin Portal|
  :Send "Create service" request to Wallet System;

  |Wallet System|
  :Validate service code uniqueness;
  :Validate service category is INTERNAL SERVICE\n(not tuition / academic tuition);
  if (Valid?) then (yes)
    :Create new service record in DB;
    :Mark service as "ACTIVE for wallet payment";
    :Return success;
  else (no)
    :Return error (duplicate code or invalid type);
  endif

  |Admin Portal|
  :Show result to System Admin;

else (no)
  if (Edit existing service?) then (yes)
    |System Admin|
    :Select existing service (e.g. CANTEEN_MEAL);
    :Edit name, owner unit,\nprice policy, active status;
    |Admin Portal|
    :Send "Update service" request to Wallet System;
    |Wallet System|
    :Validate and update service in DB;
    :Return success/failure;
    |Admin Portal|
    :Show result to System Admin;
  endif
endif

|Wallet System|
:Make updated service list available\nfor POS and internal service portals;

|Service Owner|
:Verify service appears correctly\nin their POS/portal (library/parking/canteen);

stop
@enduml
